````markdown
## Purge or Let It Expire?

```dot
digraph purge_or_expire {
    "Key's source data changed" [shape=doublecircle];
    "Would serving the stale value be wrong, not just old?\n(auth/permissions, money, a write the user just made)" [shape=diamond];
    "Will the TTL expire within the staleness this data tolerates?" [shape=diamond];
    "Purge the key now" [shape=box];
    "Let it expire. Do not purge." [shape=box];

    "Key's source data changed" -> "Would serving the stale value be wrong, not just old?\n(auth/permissions, money, a write the user just made)";
    "Would serving the stale value be wrong, not just old?\n(auth/permissions, money, a write the user just made)" -> "Purge the key now" [label="yes"];
    "Would serving the stale value be wrong, not just old?\n(auth/permissions, money, a write the user just made)" -> "Will the TTL expire within the staleness this data tolerates?" [label="no"];
    "Will the TTL expire within the staleness this data tolerates?" -> "Let it expire. Do not purge." [label="yes"];
    "Will the TTL expire within the staleness this data tolerates?" -> "Purge the key now" [label="no"];
}
```

"Data changed" alone is not a reason to purge. Purge only on a "yes" at the first question or a "no" at the second.
````

