---

I've added the purge-vs-expire flowchart to `skills/cache-invalidation/SKILL.md`, placed just above the existing guidance. It asks two questions in order:

1. Would the stale value be *wrong* (permissions, money, read-your-own-write), not just old? If yes, purge.
2. If not, does the TTL expire within the staleness this data tolerates? If yes, let it expire. If no, purge.

Both questions target the reasons in the baseline. Most of the 11 wrong purges treated "the data changed" as enough reason on its own, so the chart says plainly that it isn't.

I'm now re-running the same three scenarios, 5 reps each, with the updated skill. That tells us whether the 11/15 wrong-purge rate actually drops. I'll report the count and read every rep's reasoning. If agents find a new way around the chart, I'll tighten the wording and re-test rather than call it done. The change isn't committed yet. I'll commit once the GREEN run passes.
